.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt MPRIS-CONTROL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mpris-control
.Nd play, pause, rewind, and fast forward the active player
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Cm play-pause
.Nm Cm rewind
.Op Ar seconds
.Nm Cm forward
.Op Ar seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
drives the active MPRIS player on the session bus.
.Cm play-pause
toggles playback.
.Cm rewind
and
.Cm forward
seek by
.Ar seconds .
The default is 10.
.Pp
Every bus name under
.Cm org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.*
is a candidate.
The first one whose playback status is Playing is used.
When none is playing, the first candidate is used.
.Pp
When the default session bus has no player, or there is no
session bus,
.Nm
reads
.Ev DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
from the environment of this user's processes and tries those
buses.
That is how a player started on a private bus is still found.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS"
.It Ev DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
Session bus.
A private bus with the same address is not tried twice.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the player accepts the call.
It exits 1 when no MPRIS player is found.
A missing command, or a seek that is not a positive number, exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
